@baseUrl = https://127.0.0.1:8080
@token = paste-token-here

# Uploads need the server started with --write.
# The part name ("file") does not matter; every part with a filename is saved.

### Upload one file, creating the folder if needed
# Expect 201: {"files":[{"name":"hello.txt","path":"examples-demo/hello.txt",…}]}
# Running it a second time gives 409 "exists".
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload?path=examples-demo&mkdirs=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ExampleBoundary

--ExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hello.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./files/hello.txt
--ExampleBoundary--

### Upload several files in one request (all are saved, or none)
# Expect 201 with two entries.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload?path=examples-demo/batch&mkdirs=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ExampleBoundary

--ExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hello.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./files/hello.txt
--ExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./files/notes.md
--ExampleBoundary--

### Upload inline content, no local file needed
# Expect 201.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload?path=examples-demo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ExampleBoundary

--ExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="inline.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This file was typed straight into the request.
--ExampleBoundary--

### Replace an existing file
# Needs the server started with --overwrite, otherwise 403 "overwrite_disabled".
# Expect 201.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload?path=examples-demo&overwrite=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ExampleBoundary

--ExampleBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hello.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello again, this content replaced the original.
--ExampleBoundary--
